=== HANDLER_DIFFS ===
Architectural reality of the telemetry_*.go file set:

  The prompt body cites handler files (telemetry_climate.go, telemetry_motor.go,
  telemetry_tire_pressure.go, telemetry_security.go, telemetry_media.go) that do
  not exist in this repo. The actual API read handlers backing /climate/latest,
  /motor/latest, /tire-pressure/latest, /security/latest, /media/latest live in
  internal/api/{climate,motor,tire_pressure,security,media}_handler.go — all of
  which fall OUTSIDE the prompt's allowed-files list (internal/api/telemetry_*.go).

  The 11 in-scope telemetry_*.go files are MQTT ingest + session-tracking code
  (TelemetryHandler.ProcessSignals, TelemetrySessionTracker, alerts evaluator,
  recovery/backfill). They write through repos (PositionRepo, SecurityRepo, etc.)
  and signalHistoryWriter; they do not contain SELECTs against snapshot tables.

  Per telemetry_handler_ingest.go:652-655, repos for vehicle_live_state,
  charging_telemetry, climate_snapshots, motor_snapshots and
  vehicle_meta_snapshots have already been removed; their signals land in
  signal_log via signalHistoryWriter. No legacy non-SI column literals (e.g.
  inside_temp, outside_temp without the _c suffix; tire_pressure_psi) survive
  in any of the 11 files (verified by the gate's grep).

  Enhanced-field keys already use SI suffixes:
    enhancedFields["inside_temp_avg_c"]   (recovery + drive_tracking)
    enhancedFields["outside_temp_avg_c"]  (recovery + drive_tracking)
    enhancedFields["energy_used_kwh"]     (recovery + drive_tracking)
    enhancedFields["energy_added_kwh"]    (recovery + charge_tracking)
    enhancedFields["avg_speed_mph"], ["max_speed_mph"]
    enhancedFields["avg_power_kw"], ["regen_kwh"]
    enhancedFields["charger_power_kw_max"], ["charger_power_kw_avg"]

  Charge-state classification flows through enums.IsCharging(chargeState) — see
  telemetry_sessions_charge_tracking.go:142 — not raw enum-string equality.

  Routes preserved (router.go contract): no telemetry_*.go file owns or mutates
  /climate/latest, /motor/latest, /tire-pressure/latest, /security/latest,
  /media/latest route registrations.

Net code change inside the allowed-files set: NONE. Migration of the actual
snapshot-reader handlers (climate_handler.go etc.) belongs to a follow-on
prompt whose allowed-files list opens up internal/api/{climate,motor,
tire_pressure,security,media}_handler.go.


